          answers that are easy to scan.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq-shell" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Cat FAQ</h2>
        <p>Select a question to reveal the answer.</p>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="faq-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-1">
              <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-1">
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they feel calm and content, but they also purr to
              self-soothe when they are nervous, tired, or recovering from stress.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="faq-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-2">
              <span>How much should I feed my cat each day?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-2">
            <p>
              The right amount depends on age, weight, activity, and the food itself.
              Start with the feeding guide on the package, then adjust with your
              veterinarian if your cat is gaining or losing too much weight.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="faq-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-3">
              <span>Why does my cat knead blankets and laps?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-3">
            <p>
              Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats
              often keep doing it when they feel safe, cozy, and relaxed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="faq-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-4">
              <span>Do indoor cats still need playtime?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-4">
            <p>
              Yes. Daily play helps indoor cats exercise, practice hunting behavior, and
              avoid boredom. Short sessions with wand toys, balls, or treat puzzles can
              make a big difference.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h3>
            <button class="faq-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-5">
              <span>How often should I clean the litter box?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </h3>
          <div class="details" id="answer-5">
            <p>
              Scoop at least once a day and replace litter regularly based on the type
              you use. Clean boxes encourage good litter habits and make it easier to
              notice changes in your cat&apos;s health.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const toggles = document.querySelectorAll(".faq-toggle");

      toggles.forEach((button) => {
        const panelId = button.getAttribute("aria-controls");
        const panel = panelId ? document.getElementById(panelId) : null;

        if (!panel) {
          return;
        }

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
        panel.hidden = true;

        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
          panel.hidden = isExpanded;
        });
      });
    </script>
